            <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">Anna University Revaluation Form 2026 – Apply Online &amp; Last Date</h1>
                    <p>
                        The much-anticipated Anna University UG and PG Semester Results for the 2025-2026 academic session have been officially declared on March 13, 2026. For students who have reviewed their provisional mark sheets and believe there might be discrepancies in their evaluation, Anna University provides a crucial opportunity: the revaluation process. This guide offers comprehensive details on how to apply for the Anna University Revaluation Form 2026 online, crucial deadlines, and other vital information to ensure you don't miss out on this chance.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">What is Revaluation?</h2>
                    <p>
                        Revaluation is a procedure offered by Anna University that allows students to request a re-examination of their answer scripts if they are dissatisfied with the marks awarded or suspect an error in the initial evaluation. It's a transparent process designed to ensure fair assessment and can significantly impact a student's academic standing.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Key Dates for Anna University Revaluation 2026</h2>
                    <p>
                        Staying updated with the deadlines is paramount. Here are the important dates to keep in mind for the Anna University Revaluation process for 2026:
                    </p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Anna University UG/PG Results Declaration:</strong> March 13, 2026</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Photocopy Application Period:</strong> March 10, 2026, to March 15, 2026</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Last Date to Apply for CDE Revaluation:</strong> March 15, 2026</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Revaluation Application Period:</strong> Typically announced shortly after result declaration and after the photocopy application window closes. Students are advised to apply after reviewing their answer script photocopies.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Revaluation Results Publication:</strong> Generally within a few weeks after the application process concludes.</p>
                    </div>
                    <p class="highlight-text">
                        <strong>Critical Note:</strong> While some specific dates are available, it's crucial for students to regularly check the official Anna University examination portal at <a href="https://coe1.annauniv.edu/" target="_blank">coe1.annauniv.edu</a> for the most accurate and updated deadlines relevant to their specific course and semester.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Eligibility Criteria for Revaluation</h2>
                    <p>
                        Any student who is not satisfied with their marks or believes there has been an error in the evaluation of their answer script is eligible to apply for revaluation. This includes cases where students suspect totaling mistakes, omitted valuations, or other discrepancies.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Anna University Revaluation &amp; Photocopy Fees 2026</h2>
                    <p>
                        Applicants need to pay a prescribed fee for both the photocopy of the answer script and for revaluation. The fees are generally non-refundable.
                    </p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Service</th>
                                <th>Approximate Fee (Per Subject)</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Photocopy of Answer Script</td>
                                <td>Rs. 300</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Revaluation Application</td>
                                <td>Rs. 300 - Rs. 750 (varies by course/regulation)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                    <p>
                        For CDE results, the revaluation fee is Rs. 300. It is always recommended to verify the exact fees on the official university notification before making any payments.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">How to Apply Online for Anna University Revaluation Form 2026: Step-by-Step Guide</h2>
                    <p>
                        The application process for revaluation is primarily conducted online through the Controller of Examinations (COE) portal. Follow these steps carefully:
                    </p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official COE Portal</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Go to the official Anna University examination portal: <a href="https://coe1.annauniv.edu/" target="_blank">coe1.annauniv.edu</a>.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Navigate to the Revaluation Section</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            On the homepage, look for the 'Examination Services' or 'Revaluation' section. This might be prominently displayed or found under a 'Student Services' tab.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Login with Credentials</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            You may need to log in using your Registration Number and Date of Birth to access the revaluation application form.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. Select Subjects for Revaluation</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Carefully select the subject(s) for which you wish to apply for revaluation. Ensure you enter the correct subject codes and names.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">5. Fill in Required Details</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            The online form will require details such as your college code, name, semester/year, and other personal information. Double-check all entered data for accuracy.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">6. Upload Necessary Documents (if any)</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            While online applications generally don't require extensive document uploads initially, be prepared to provide any supporting information if requested.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">7. Pay the Revaluation Fee</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Proceed to pay the prescribed revaluation fee online through the available payment gateways. Keep a record of your transaction ID.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">8. Submit the Application</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            After reviewing all the details and ensuring the payment is successful, submit your revaluation application. Download and print the confirmation page for your records.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Important Information Required for Application</h2>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ Your Anna University Registration Number</p>
                        <p>✅ Date of Birth</p>
                        <p>✅ College Code</p>
                        <p>✅ Semester/Year of the Examination</p>
                        <p>✅ Correct Subject Code(s) and Name(s) for Revaluation</p>
                        <p>✅ Valid Email ID and Mobile Number for communication</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">What Happens After Applying?</h2>
                    <p>
                        Once your revaluation application is successfully submitted, the university will undertake the re-evaluation of your chosen answer script(s). The revaluation results are typically published on the same official result portal within a few weeks of the application process being completed. Students are advised to keep checking the portal for updates.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Final Thoughts</h2>
                    <p>
                        The revaluation process is a valuable option for Anna University students to ensure their academic performance is accurately reflected. Given that the results for 2026 are out, and the photocopy application window is closing soon, prompt action is essential. Do not delay in checking the official website for the precise deadlines and application procedures to avoid missing this critical opportunity.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
